A||||1||Neal||SI Valves?||||5||
Z||000000||Neal||06-05-2001||02:30 PM||||Are the SI valves from the fiero store worth it?<P>Will i see any kind of gains over a standard stock valve.<P>And if i makes a difference i will not be porting the head beyond gasket matching.||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||06-05-2001||04:38 PM||||The SI valves are swirl polished, tuliped, and don’t have as much throat sticking into the ports like the OEM valves do causing a restriction. They should flow better than OEM valves do. When I bought mine I had a performance valve job done to the heads and I had the machinist undercut the VALVES (put another angle on them) for improved low lift flow. If you want to gain more torque and horsepower than you should have the bowl area blended on the intake port and have the exhaust ports polished and blended. Don’t make the ports bigger and don’t remove the hump in the intake port. <P>The heads, camshaft, intake system, and exhaust system are where all the power lies, the rest is just for durability. The heads and camshaft are especially important.    <P><BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 06-05-2001).]||||reg||1
